codex
The new static migration guard has a bypass for valid SQLite UPDATE syntax, so it does not fully enforce the invariant it introduces. It also over-rejects trigger SQL on similarly named non-canonical tables.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Handle SQLite UPDATE conflict clauses — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1228-1230
  For migrations that use SQLite's valid `UPDATE OR <conflict-action>` syntax, e.g. `UPDATE OR REPLACE canonical_nodes SET logical_id = ...`, the guard extracts `OR` as the table name and returns `false`, so a forbidden `logical_id` backfill can bypass the TC-11 pin. The table extractor needs to skip the optional conflict clause before comparing against the pinned canonical tables.

- [P3] Avoid substring matching trigger targets — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1283-1285
  For triggers on non-canonical tables whose names contain a pinned table name, such as `canonical_nodes_backup`, this substring check rejects the migration even though it does not target `canonical_nodes` or `canonical_edges`. That makes legitimate recreate/backup trigger scaffolding fail the pin; the trigger path should identify table tokens the same way the other arms do rather than using `contains`.
The new static migration guard has a bypass for valid SQLite UPDATE syntax, so it does not fully enforce the invariant it introduces. It also over-rejects trigger SQL on similarly named non-canonical tables.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Handle SQLite UPDATE conflict clauses — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1228-1230
  For migrations that use SQLite's valid `UPDATE OR <conflict-action>` syntax, e.g. `UPDATE OR REPLACE canonical_nodes SET logical_id = ...`, the guard extracts `OR` as the table name and returns `false`, so a forbidden `logical_id` backfill can bypass the TC-11 pin. The table extractor needs to skip the optional conflict clause before comparing against the pinned canonical tables.

- [P3] Avoid substring matching trigger targets — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1283-1285
  For triggers on non-canonical tables whose names contain a pinned table name, such as `canonical_nodes_backup`, this substring check rejects the migration even though it does not target `canonical_nodes` or `canonical_edges`. That makes legitimate recreate/backup trigger scaffolding fail the pin; the trigger path should identify table tokens the same way the other arms do rather than using `contains`.
